{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"733","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Drivers Dissatisfaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one kingdom there are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cities and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" two-way roads. Each road connects a pair of cities, and for each road we know the level of drivers dissatisfaction — the value "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"wi"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each road we know the value "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" — how many lamziks we should spend to reduce the level of dissatisfaction with this road by one. Thus, to reduce the dissatisfaction with the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th road by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":", we should spend "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k·ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" lamziks. And "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"it is allowed for the dissatisfaction to become zero or even negative"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In accordance with the king's order, we need to choose "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" roads and make them the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"main roads"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". An important condition must hold: it should be possible to travel from any city to any other by the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"main roads"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The road ministry has a budget of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" lamziks for the reform. The ministry is going to spend this budget for repair of some roads (to reduce the dissatisfaction with them), and then to choose the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"main roads"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help to spend the budget in such a way and then to choose the main roads so that the total dissatisfaction with the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"main roads"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be as small as possible. The dissatisfaction with some roads can become negative. It is not necessary to spend whole budget "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that it is possible to travel from any city to any other using existing roads. Each road in the kingdom is a two-way road."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 2·105"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1 ≤ m ≤ 2·105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of cities and the number of roads in the kingdom, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w1, w2, ..., wm"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ wi ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"wi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the drivers dissatisfaction with the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th road."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c1, c2, ..., cm"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ci ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the cost (in lamziks) of reducing the dissatisfaction with the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th road by one."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the description of the roads. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of this lines contain a pair of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai, bi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai ≠ bi"},{"kind":"text","text":") which mean that the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th road connects cities "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":". All roads are two-way oriented so it is possible to move by the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th road from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":", and vice versa. It is allowed that a pair of cities is connected by more than one road. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The last line contains one integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ S ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of lamziks which we can spend for reforms. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"K"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the minimum possible total dissatisfaction with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"main roads"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines print two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x, vx"},{"kind":"text","text":", which mean that the road "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" is among main roads and the road "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":", after the reform, has the level of dissatisfaction "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vx"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider that roads are numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the order as they are given in the input data. The edges can be printed in arbitrary order. If there are several answers, print any of them. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6 9\n1 3 1 1 3 1 2 2 2\n4 1 4 2 2 5 3 1 6\n1 2\n1 3\n2 3\n2 4\n2 5\n3 5\n3 6\n4 5\n5 6\n7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n1 1\n3 1\n6 1\n7 2\n8 -5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 3\n9 5 1\n7 7 2\n2 1\n3 1\n3 2\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n3 0\n2 5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"733F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/733/problem/F"}